The map is cut into small blocks;
each keeps one summary number,
so the map becomes smaller.

lec06kp03-u01-p6-nf-lec06-kp03-p6-60.text:
Reading $[6,4]$: the bottom edge lies in the lower half.
The windows of the left half lie entirely on it, so $6$;
those of the right half cover only part of it, so $4$.

lec06kp03-u01-p13-nf-lec06-kp03-p13-23.text:
$x=[1,-3,2,5,-4]$: slide the kernel $[1,1]$, multiply and add;
then apply $[1,-1]$ and compare with one pass of $[1,0,-1]$.
With a ReLU in between, is it still the same?
